xpect  any president to brag about job growth  whether or not they had a hand in it it  is still a good thing but it is  important to understand the context  many of these jobs would be coming back  regardless of who was president i'd  rather it be joe biden than donald trump  for sure  joe biden then jumping right into  talking about the economy and talking  about  the importance of unions much to bernie  sanders delight  and unions built the middle class  that's why i'm calling on congress  to pass protect the right to organize  act the pro act and send it to my desk  so we can support  the right to unionize  and by the way and joe biden then  much to the pleasure of most democrats  in the crowd but not mitt romney  and lauren beaubert and others saying  let's raise the minimum wage to fifteen  dollars an hour  let's raise the minimum wage to fifteen  dollars  no one  no one working 40 hours a week  no one working 40 hours a week should  live below the poverty line  we need to ensure greater equity and  opportunity for women and while we're  doing this let's get the paycheck  fairness act to my desk as well  equal pay they spent much too long  and if you wonder whether it's too long  look behind me  joe biden also laying out how he will  pay for  much of these ideas saying the rich will  pay and mitt romney didn't seem  particularly thrilled with that either  time for corporate america  and the wealthiest one percent of  americans have just begun to pay their  fair share  just their fair share  [Music]  sometimes i have arguments with my  friends in the democratic party  i think you should be able to become a  billionaire and a millionaire but pay  your fair share and on economics a  moment  that many people liked which got a lot  of attention  joe biden saying straight up trickle  down  economics has never worked  my fellow americans trickle down  trickle down economics has never worked  and it's time to grow the economy from  the bottom in the middle out  you know now i love this because  i already planned later today to talk  about  joe biden and biodynamics as they are  being called  as the antithesis to reaganomics  that line trickle-down economics has  never worked  is actually part of it saying it as  directly as anybody can and we're going  to come back to that in more detail  on foreign policy joe biden pointing out  that  he's just getting out of afghanistan  something that republicans  loved when it was trump who announced it  trump failed to do it  joe biden is doing it and republicans  are no longer clapping about it  stern deterrence and american leadership  means ending the forever war in  afghanistan  we have  we have without hyperbole the greatest  fighting force in history of the world  i'm the first president of 40 years and  knows what it means to have a son  serving in a war zone today we have  service members serving in the same war  zone as their parents did  we have service members in afghanistan  who are not yet born  on 9 11. the war in afghanistan as we  remember the debates here  were never meant to be  multi-generational undertakings  of nation building of course it was  never really about  just getting out of afghanistan it was  can we cheer for something trump is  doing  biden now is actually going to do the  thing we cheered trump for announcing  but we don't cheer anymore  because we are merely political  hypocrites real quick here is senator  ted cruz  sleeping during the speech he looked  very very sleepy apparently dreaming of  cancun  and joe biden ultimately closing out  his speech take a listen to that it's  never  ever ever been a good bet to bet against  america  and it still isn't we're the united  states of america  there's not a single thing nothing  nothing beyond our capacity  we can do whatever we set our mind to if  we do it together  so let's begin to get together  god bless you all and may god protect  our troops  thank you for your patience  some of the people in the camp of biden  is a weakling and he's old and senile  and demented we're expecting a very  short speech  and a very incoherent speech biden going  much longer than recent presidents have  during their first joint addresses to  congress  and very coherent i thought it was a  well-written speech  i thought it was about the right  duration i often think things are too  long i think it was about the right  duration  and now actually comes the tough part  which is joe biden has laid out a  variety of different policy ideas  can joe biden get any of what he  proposed  done and that is certainly easier said  than done when not only do you have  zero republican support in the house and  senate for  anything you want to do but it's not  even clear you have the support of all  of the democrats in the senate either  and we will talk about that as these  proposals become more formalized and  start to be debated  one of our sponsors today is covid  rescue  fund covid rescue fund is helping small  business owners  who have lost their businesses during  covid  there are over 100 000 small businesses  that have had to close their doors since  the pandemic began  there are many organizations out there  helping businesses who are still  open to stay afloat but covet rescue  fund is one of the few organizations  working to help  businesses reopen who have had to close  covet rescue fund crowdsources funds to  provide  grants up to one hundred thousand  dollars for these owners to create  new businesses i would implore anyone in  my audience to help covet rescue fund  in their mission by donating at  covidrescufund.org  all money that you give is going to the  mission  not to compensating people who work for  the organization  the founders of covid rescue fund are  big fans of the david pakman show  let's help them bring back as many small  businesses  as we can the link is right underneath  this video
 

